d Bracelet Price Guide Price depends on total carat weight, diamond shape, gold karatage, and setting style. Simple prong-set styles in 14KT gold sit at the accessible end of the range, while higher carat tennis bracelets in 18KT gold with bezel settings sit higher. Prices are subject to change based on prevailing gold rates. How to Choose the Right Lab Grown Diamond Bracelet Start with how often you plan to wear it. For daily wear, a lower profile prong or bezel setting in 14KT gold resists everyday knocks well. For occasion pieces, a higher carat tennis bracelet or a bracelet with fancy-shape diamonds makes more of a statement. Wrist size matters too: most Lucira bracelets are available from 5 inch to 7 inch lengths, and our sizing guide on each product page can help you confirm fit before ordering. Certification and Trust Every lab grown diamond bracelet at Lucira is IGI or SGL certified, and all gold is BIS hallmarked. Lucira also offers a 90% lifetime buyback and 100% lifetime exchange on eligible pieces, along with in-person support at our experience centres in Mumbai, Pune, and Noida. Frequently Asked Questions Is a lab grown diamond bracelet worth buying?Yes, for buyers who want genuine diamond brilliance without the premium of a mined stone. Lab grown diamonds offer the same hardness, sparkle, and durability as mined diamonds at a comparatively lower price point, making them a practical choice for everyday jewellery. How much does a lab grown diamond bracelet cost?Cost depends on carat weight, diamond shape, gold karatage, and setting complexity. Simpler designs in 14KT gold sit at the lower end, while higher carat tennis bracelets in 18KT gold cost more. Exact pricing is available on each product page and is subject to change based on gold rates. How do I clean a lab grown diamond bracelet?Use lukewarm water with a mild soap, a soft-bristle brush for gentle cleaning around the setting, and a soft cloth to dry. Avoid harsh chemicals and remove the bracelet before swimming or exercising. What carat weight should I choose for a bracelet?For everyday wear, lower total carat weight in a secure prong or bezel setting tends to hold up better against daily knocks. For occasion wear, a higher carat tennis bracelet makes more of a visual statement. Does Lucira offer buyback or exchange on bracelets?Yes, eligible Lucira bracelets come with a 90% lifetime buyback and 100% lifetime exchange policy. Terms are confirmed at the time of purchase and may vary by collection.

